# Luminary — V2i onboarding dance
- date: 2026-09-27
- branch: fix/cli-254-v2i-onboarding-dance
- lead: john-ousterhout
- supporting: [michael-feathers, alan-cooper]

## Ousterhout (lead) — deep module
The dance sits inside drive_start with a narrow interface (one env var,
one behavior toggle). Callers do not learn about picker screens, sleep
values, or expect-Tcl syntax. drive_start hides all of that. The
5-verb interface stays 5 verbs.

## Feathers (supporting) — characterization
The dance is characterized by 5 Tier 0 tests that pin its queue-file
output shape. If a future Claude release changes the onboarding flow,
these tests still pass (they check what the dance emits, not what
Claude renders). Drive.log stays the source of truth for the flow.

## Cooper (supporting) — real operator state
Real operators do not sit through the theme picker every session.
Their machines have theme + acceptance state already. The dance
matches that reality inside the ephemeral Docker container.
